{
 "_about": [
  "The stat block line grammar (ROADMAP #74, Phase 1), as expected results for one line at a time.",
  "The full rules, and the formats they serve, are 'reading_rules' in statblock_formats.json; this file checks them line by line. Where the two disagree, statblock_formats.json wins.",
  "Each case gives the raw source line (before inline markup and smart punctuation: classify FIRST, then inline each part, the way table cells are split before _inline) and where it sits: 'head' (before the end of the head: the line after a Challenge, CR or Proficiency Bonus field, a section heading, or a named entry) or 'section' (after it).",
  "kind is one of: field {label, value} | fields {fields: [{label, value}]} | scores {cells: [{name, score, mod, save?}], auto} | section {name} | entry {text, name?} | ignore (a wrapper line: rules, {{monster, }}, a lone ':'). Multi-line score shapes (a names line then a values line; a Markdown table) are block-level and live in statblock_formats.md.",
  "mod is the modifier as printed, with a true minus sign (U+2212) for negatives; auto is true when the modifiers were worked out rather than written.",
  "All the open questions were decided by the user on 2026-10-07; see 'Decided' in README.md."
 ],
